      "id": "chk_1001",
      "documentId": "doc_001",
      "chunkIndex": 12,
      "content": "### 3.2 Heuristic Search Strategies: The A* Algorithm\n\nThe most widely known form of best-first search is called **A* search**. It evaluates nodes by combining $g(n)$, the cost to reach the node, and $h(n)$, the cost to get from the node to the goal:\n\n$$f(n) = g(n) + h(n)$$\n\nSince $g(n)$ gives the path cost from the start node to node $n$, and $h(n)$ is the estimated cost of the cheapest path from $n$ to the goal, we have $f(n) =$ estimated cost of the cheapest solution through $n$.",
      "tokenCount": 138,
      "characterCount": 492,
      "metadata": {
        "pageStart": 45,
        "pageEnd": 46,
        "sectionPath": ["Chapter 3: Solving Problems by Searching", "3.2 Informed Search Strategies", "A* Search"],
        "headingLevel": 3,
        "hasTable": false,
        "hasEquation": true,
        "imageRefs": []
      },
      "createdAt": "2026-10-15T09:12:00Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "chk_1002",
      "documentId": "doc_001",
      "chunkIndex": 13,
      "content": "### Conditions for Optimality: Admissibility and Consistency\n\nThe first condition we require for optimality is that $h(n)$ be an **admissible heuristic**. An admissible heuristic is one that never overestimates the cost to reach the goal.\n\n| Property | Tree Search Requirement | Graph Search Requirement |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Optimality Condition | Admissible ($h(n) \\le h^*(n)$) | Consistent ($h(n) \\le c(n, a, n') + h(n')$) |\n| Completeness | Yes (if step cost $\\ge \\epsilon > 0$) | Yes |\n| Time Complexity | $O(b^d)$ | $O(b^d)$ |",
      "tokenCount": 175,
      "characterCount": 580,
